                <pb facs="0669" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">251.11 Insull, Samuel/347: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-05T13:00:00+02:00">March 5, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 5—9:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Your 13, March 3, 2 p.m. The Foreign Minister telephoned me this morning that
                    the Minister of the Interior would today direct the fugitive to leave Greek
                    territory immediately.</p>
                <p>Following this the Minister of the Interior informed the press that he has sent a
                    police officer to Insull with an order to leave tomorrow. He further stated that
                    Insull would travel on a Greek <hi rendition="#italic">laissez passer.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
